{
  "name": "Shadow Courier — Tier 1: Liminal Operator",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/sundries/documents/envelope-letter-post.webp",
  "system": {
    "category": "technique",
    "source": "Bad Eden Bulwark + Shadow Courier v1.0 (RFI-native rules)",
    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>You cross what isn't supposed to be crossed — and you always come out the other side carrying something.</em></p><p><strong>On gaining Shadow Courier Initiation 1 you receive:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Skill rank +1 in <strong>Stealth (Intrigue)</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Skill rank +1 in <strong>Tinkering (Intrigue)</strong>.</p></li><li><p><strong>+20 Intrigue marks</strong> and <strong>+20 Logistics marks</strong> to your Domain's caps.</p></li><li><p>You bank <strong>Surge</strong> by moving: 6 squares on your turn banks +1, again at 12 (max +2 a round).</p></li><li><p><strong>Package</strong> slot comes online — one Package at a time, type set by your chosen Route at L1.</p></li></ul><p>Spend Surge from the ◆ Surge menu: Snap Strike, Flank &amp; Strike, Clear Road, Quiet Voyage and your Route's spends.</p><p><strong>Liminal Sense.</strong> Once a scene, ignore the first detection-style roll an opponent attempts against you (perception, scrying, Insight to read your intent, etc.). The roll is treated as if it had failed; resources spent on the attempt are not refunded.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
